      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a fair point. I guess I'm just thinking about the optics too. When we talk about \"culturally distinct\" in these high-level roles, it often implies a different background that might not resonate with our client base, who are mostly very traditional. Do you think there's a correlation between a candidate's ability to navigate these elite, established circles and their actual capacity for high-level leadership in this specific industry?",
